## What goes here eventually

Replace this entire file with the full text of the chosen license, and add the
matching SPDX identifier as a `"license"` field in `.claude-plugin/plugin.json`
(for example `"license": "MIT"` or `"license": "Apache-2.0"`).

Candidates worth weighing:

| License | Why you'd pick it |
|---------|-------------------|
| **MIT** | Shortest and most permissive; the common default for tooling meant to be widely adopted. |
| **Apache-2.0** | Same permissiveness as MIT plus an explicit patent grant and a trademark clause — the safer pick if organisations will adopt this. |
| **CC BY 4.0** | Built for prose/documentation rather than code; worth considering because much of this repo is written method guidance. |

### A note on the source material

This project encodes the **publicly documented** SEI methodology — ADD 3.0, ATAM,
QAW, and Views-and-Beyond — expressed in original prose. The underlying books and
SEI technical reports listed under **Sources** in [`README.md`](README.md) remain
the copyright of their respective authors and publishers; whichever license is
chosen here applies only to this repository's own text, templates, and code.
